    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d60">

                <pb facs="0100" n="90" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg90"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 E.A.C./9–1944</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-19">September 19, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The French Delegate<anchor n="95" xml:id="d60-f1"/> called at his request. He
                    said that his “Government” desired first to thank this Government for turning
                    back to him and his associates the French embassy for reoccupation by
                        them.<anchor n="96" xml:id="d60-f2"/>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0101" n="91" xml:id="pg91"/>
                <p>He then handed me a note, copy of which is hereto attached,<anchor n="97"
                        xml:id="d60-f3"/> relating to the desires of the present French authorities
                    in France to be placed on the European Advisory Commission in London.</p>
                <p>I thanked him and said the matter would be given early and full attention, and
                    that I would confer with my associates and pass it on to the President.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ull</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d60-f1" n="95" xml:id="d60-f1-content">
                <p>Henri Hoppenot, Delegate of the French Committee of National Liberation and later
                    of the French Provisional Government.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d60-f2" n="96" xml:id="d60-f2-content">
                <p>For correspondence regarding the recognition by the United States of the French
                    Provisional Government on October 23, 1944, see <ref target="frus1944v03#pg_634"
                        >vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, pp. 634</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d60-f3" n="97" xml:id="d60-f3-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Infra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
